MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Makes the per-settlement lighting/item system something a settler can actually
shape, and closes a gap where earned certificates never produced a visible object.

Settlement design authoring (src/lib/settlement-items.ts, SettlementInventory.vue):
- add updateItem(); expandable per-item controls for colour and zone, the first
  UI ever built against recolouring (placeItem existed but was never called)
- theme packs (src/data/theme-packs.ts): curated bundles of existing presets,
  applied in one action. Colours come from themePackItemColorHex(), derived from
  the settlement's own hue, so a pack belongs to that settlement rather than
  dropping in a stock palette
- peer-to-peer design sharing via gift codes, reusing the existing site-wide
  storage cipher (fixed seed, so a code made in one browser decodes in another).
  Carries attribution (donorName) — no price, cart, or transfer of ownership,
  keeping the resale-risk posture this repo already paid down
- presets attesting real-world work (decon site marker, community monument) are
  deliberately not shareable; the starter lantern stays unclonable

Rewards → visible objects (RewardsPage.vue, rewards-catalog.ts):
- attachObject() now also places a real lit mesh via addItem(), following the
  pattern in PfasCitizenSciencePage.vue. Previously an earned certificate only
  pushed a string onto SettlementRecord.objects[] and nothing appeared in the dome
- new 'reward' acquisition type, kept out of the acquire picker so an earned
  object can't be self-granted

Correctness/scale:
- addItem() now enforces the preset's acquiredBy list structurally; it was only
  ever a UI filter, so a direct call could add any type/preset pair
- cap dynamic point lights at 12 (MAX_ITEM_LIGHTS); later items still render in
  full, they just stop adding real-time shading passes

Also includes prior in-progress work already present in the working tree
(docs, legal copy, community-nodes routing, onboarding and admin changes).

