+Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: single source of truth for resonance split; correct
+ wrong figures in deed hash and glossary
+
+The same concept was stated with four different sets of numbers:
+99/0.75/0.25 (DocsPage, DocPage, DocPage0, erc721-metadata, mint-style),
+80/15/5 (GlossaryPage summary, SettlementHashmark), 80/10/0 (GlossaryPage
+body, contradicting its own summary line), and 100/0/0 (exoloc settlement
+deed written by MintPage).
+
+Two of those were reaching immutable records. SettlementHashmark's 80/15/5
+sits inside the object SHA-256'd into design_hash, which is embedded in
+ERC-721 deed metadata - a permanent misstatement about where money goes,
+attached to an artefact a user paid gas to create.
+
+- New src/lib/resonance-split.ts holds STANDARD_SPLIT (99/0.75/0.25) and
+  SETTLEMENT_SPLIT (100/0/0). No on-chain value changes: every metadata
+  writer keeps the figure it already wrote.
+- SettlementHashmark corrected 80/15/5 -> SETTLEMENT_SPLIT. Hashmark schema
+  bumped v1 -> v2 so previously minted deed hashes stay reproducible under
+  the schema they were minted with.
+- GlossaryPage entry 31 rewritten: it stated 80/15/5 in the summary and
+  80/10/0 in the body, and matched no shipped writer.
+- DocsPage/DocPage0/DocPage no longer claim the standard split applies to
+  'all transactions' - settlement deeds differ and primary minting is free,
+  so on that path there is no fee to divide.
+- Added PRIMARY_MINT_IS_FREE with a note: quoting a split next to a free
+  mint implies a revenue stream that does not exist.
