+From 4b368574ba30ab5becd1965e9d47bad864ed45ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: exotopia <dev@exotopia.org>
+Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 05:32:49 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): lock down reward ledger writes; pin
+ search_path on definer functions
+
+Migration 007. Two issues held back from the cleanup pass because neither is
+cleanup.
+
+(A) search_path. Five-plus SECURITY DEFINER functions in public had no
+    search_path pinned. A definer function resolves unqualified names using the
+    caller's search_path, so a caller able to create objects in an earlier
+    schema can shadow a referenced table or operator and have it run with the
+    definer's privileges. Pinned via ALTER FUNCTION in a DO block over
+    pg_proc.prosecdef, so no function body is rewritten and functions added
+    later are covered too.
+
+(B) The reward ledger was self-serve. reward_events_insert allowed
+    WITH CHECK (member_id = auth.uid() OR is_admin()) and points had only
+    CHECK (points >= 0). The anon key is public and RLS was the only gate, so
+    any authenticated user could POST to PostgREST with arbitrary points and
+    skip the app. certificates_insert had the same shape - a user could
+    self-issue 'mentorship', which compliance/digital-credentials-law frames as
+    carrying real-world standing. All of mentor_session_guard()'s anti-fraud
+    work was bypassable by inserting the reward row directly.
+
+    Clients lose INSERT on both tables. Awards now go through definer RPCs:
+    - points_catalog / quiz_reward_rules hold point values, caps and quiz
+      thresholds server-side
+    - award_self_reported() sets points from the catalogue, enforces a per
+      action daily cap, and marks rows self_reported so audits can tell
+      asserted work from verified work
+    - award_quiz_completion() enforces threshold, prerequisite chain and the
+      one-shot rule
+    - refresh_certificates() derives certificates from ledger state; it is the
+      only issuance path and is not client-executable
+    - unique indexes kill replay of quiz awards and duplicate certificates
+    - mentor pair cooldown + unique (mentor, mentee, topic) bounds the
+      two-account collusion loop
+    - admin_members no longer readable by anonymous visitors
+
+    src/stores/rewards.ts migrated to the RPCs; without this the app breaks on
+    deploy, since the INSERT paths it relied on are gone.
